  "title": "LuckRead Media API Operation Policy",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "domain": "media",
  "greenRule": "Media is production-green only when upload, asset ownership, processing state, delivery authorization, retention, resource budgets, abuse controls and runtime E2E evidence all pass.",
  "invariants": [
    "Large media bytes MUST NOT be buffered fully in a Worker.",
    "Upload and download data paths MUST use bounded streaming or direct object-storage transfer.",
    "Media metadata is authoritative in platform storage; object bytes are authoritative in R2/object storage.",
    "Every externally retried upload mutation MUST be idempotent by operation key or immutable asset identity.",
    "Processing jobs MUST be bounded by size, duration, variant count, retry count and output bytes.",
    "Signed delivery credentials MUST be short-lived, resource-scoped and revocable by policy.",
    "Delete and retention operations MUST NOT synchronously fan out to unbounded physical objects.",
    "A failed processing attempt MUST NOT create an additional authoritative media asset."
  ],
